#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:1
msgid "Use ROS 2 to interact with Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:3
msgid ""
"In this tutorial we will learn how to use ROS 2 to communicate with Gazebo.  "
"This can help in many aspects; we can receive data (like joint states, TFs) "
"or commands from ROS and apply it to Gazebo and vice versa. This can also "
"help to enable RViz to visualize a robot model simultaneously simulated by a "
"Gazebo world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:8
msgid "ros_gz_bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:10
msgid ""
"[`ros_gz_bridge`](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz) provides a network "
"bridge which enables the exchange of messages between ROS 2 and [Gazebo "
"Transport](https://github.com/gazebosim/gz-transport). Its support is "
"limited to only certain message types. Please, check this [README](https://"
"github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md) to verify if "
"your message type is supported by the bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:12
msgid ""
"Example uses of the bridge can be found in [`ros_gz_sim_demos`](https://"
"github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/tree/ros2/ros_gz_sim_demos), including demo "
"launch files with bridging of all major actuation and sensor types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:14
msgid "Launching the bridge manually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:16
msgid ""
"We can initialize a bidirectional bridge so we can have ROS as the publisher "
"and Gazebo as the subscriber or vice versa. The syntax is `/"
"TOPIC@ROS_MSG@GZ_MSG`, such that `TOPIC` is the Gazebo internal topic, "
"`ROS_MSG` is the ROS message type for this topic, and `GZ_MSG` is the Gazebo "
"message type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:18
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:20
msgid ""
"ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge /scan@sensor_msgs/msg/LaserScan@gz."
"msgs.LaserScan\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:24
msgid ""
"The `ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge` command simply runs the "
"`parameter_bridge` code from the `ros_gz_bridge` package. Then, we specify "
"our topic `/TOPIC` over which the messages will be sent. The first `@` "
"symbol delimits the topic name from the message types. Following the first "
"`@` symbol is the ROS message type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:26
msgid "The ROS message type is followed by an `@`, `[`, or `]` symbol where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:28
msgid "`@`  is a bidirectional bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:29
msgid "`[`  is a bridge from Gazebo to ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:30
msgid "`]`  is a bridge from ROS to Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:32
msgid ""
"Have a look at these [examples]( https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/"
"ros2/ros_gz_bridge/README.md#example-1a-gazebo-transport-talker-and-ros-2-"
"listener) explaining how to make communication connections from ROS to "
"Gazebo and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:35
msgid ""
"It is also possible to use ROS Launch with the `ros_gz_bridge` and represent "
"the topics in yaml format to be given to the bridge at launch time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:37
msgid ""
"- ros_topic_name: \"scan\"\n"
"  gz_topic_name: \"/scan\"\n"
"  ros_type_name: \"sensor_msgs/msg/LaserScan\"\n"
"  gz_type_name: \"gz.msgs.LaserScan\"\n"
"  direction: GZ_TO_ROS  # BIDIRECTIONAL or ROS_TO_GZ\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:45
msgid ""
"The configuration file is a YAML file that contains the mapping between the "
"ROS and Gazebo topics to be bridged. For each pair of topics to be bridged, "
"the following parameters are accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:49
msgid "`ros_topic_name`: The topic name on the ROS side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:50
msgid "`gz_topic_name`: The corresponding topic name on the Gazebo side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:51
msgid "`ros_type_name`: The type of this ROS topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:52
msgid "`gz_type_name`: The type of this Gazebo topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:53
msgid "`subscriber_queue`: The size of the ROS subscriber queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:54
msgid "`publisher_queue`: The size of the ROS publisher queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:55
msgid ""
"`lazy`: Whether there's a lazy subscriber or not. If there's no real "
"subscribers the bridge won't create the internal subscribers either. This "
"should speedup performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:58
msgid ""
"`direction`: It's possible to specify `GZ_TO_ROS`, `ROS_TO_GZ` and "
"`BIDIRECTIONAL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:61
msgid ""
"See [this example](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/ros2/"
"ros_gz_bridge/test/config/full.yaml) for a valid configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:64
msgid ""
"Launching the bridge using the launch files included in `ros_gz_bridge` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:66
msgid ""
"The package `ros_gz_bridge` contains a launch file named `ros_gz_bridge."
"launch.py`. You can use it to start a ROS 2 and Gazebo bridge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:69
msgid "Here's an example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:70
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_bridge ros_gz_bridge.launch.py bridge_name:=ros_gz_bridge "
"config_file:=<path_to_your_YAML_file>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:74
msgid "Launching with composition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:75
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_bridge ros_gz_bridge.launch.py bridge_name:=ros_gz_bridge "
"config_file:=<path_to_your_YAML_file> use_composition:=True "
"create_own_container:=True\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:78
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if an existing container is already running, you can pass its "
"name when launching the bridge using the `container_name` parameter. More "
"info about composition can be viewed [here](ros2_overview.md#composition)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:81
msgid ""
"Check [this block](https://github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/jazzy/"
"ros_gz_bridge/launch/ros_gz_bridge.launch.py#L25-L68) from the source code "
"to know all the different parameters accepted by this launch file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:85
msgid "QOS Overrides:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:87
msgid ""
"QOS overrides can be passed as extra parameters to the bridge using the "
"`bridge_params` argument of the launch file. An example of this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:88
msgid ""
"ros2 launch ros_gz_bridge ros_gz_bridge.launch.py bridge_name:=ros_gz_bridge "
"config_file:=<path_to_your_YAML_file> bridge_params:={'qos_overrides./"
"topic_name.publisher.durability': 'transient_local', 'qos_overrides./"
"another_topic_name.publisher.durability': 'transient_local'}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:91
msgid ""
"You can omit the following from what you pass to `bridge_params`: `{}`, ` `, "
"`\"`, `'`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:93
msgid ""
"More info about using QOS overrides can be found [here](https://docs.ros.org/"
"en/jazzy/How-To-Guides/Overriding-QoS-Policies-For-Recording-And-Playback."
"html#using-qos-overrides)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:95
msgid "Launching the bridge from a custom launch file in XML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:97
msgid ""
"It's also possible to trigger the bridge from your custom launch file. For "
"that purpose we have created the `<ros_gz_bridge/>` tag that can be used "
"from you XML or YAML launch file. In this case, the arguments are passed as "
"attributes within this tag. Here's a simplified example, a more "
"comprehensive example can be viewed [here](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"ros_gz/blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/launch/ros_gz_bridge.launch):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:102
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <arg name=\"bridge_name\" />\n"
"  <arg name=\"config_file\" />\n"
"  <ros_gz_bridge\n"
"    bridge_name=\"$(var bridge_name)\"\n"
"    config_file=\"$(var config_file)\">\n"
"  </ros_gz_bridge>\n"
"</launch>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:113
msgid ""
"In this case the `<ros_gz_bridge>` parameters are read from the command "
"line. That's an option but not strictly necessary as you could decide to "
"hardcode some of the values or not even use all the parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:117
msgid "Launching the bridge from a custom launch file in Python."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:119
msgid ""
"Here's a simplified example of a Python launch file used to load a bridge "
"from Python, a more comprehensive example can be viewed [here](https://"
"github.com/gazebosim/ros_gz/blob/ros2/ros_gz_bridge/launch/ros_gz_bridge."
"launch.py):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:121
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"from launch.actions import DeclareLaunchArgument\n"
"from launch.substitutions import LaunchConfiguration, TextSubstitution\n"
"from ros_gz_bridge.actions import RosGzBridge\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"\n"
"    bridge_name = LaunchConfiguration('bridge_name')\n"
"    config_file = LaunchConfiguration('config_file')\n"
"\n"
"    declare_bridge_name_cmd = DeclareLaunchArgument(\n"
"        'bridge_name', description='Name of ros_gz_bridge node'\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"    declare_config_file_cmd = DeclareLaunchArgument(\n"
"        'config_file', description='YAML config file'\n"
"    )\n"
"\n"
"    # Create the launch description and populate\n"
"    ld = LaunchDescription([\n"
"        RosGzBridge(\n"
"            bridge_name=LaunchConfiguration('bridge_name'),\n"
"            config_file=LaunchConfiguration('config_file'),\n"
"        ),\n"
"    ])\n"
"\n"
"    # Declare the launch options\n"
"    ld.add_action(declare_bridge_name_cmd)\n"
"    ld.add_action(declare_config_file_cmd)\n"
"\n"
"    return ld\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:156
msgid "Publish key strokes to ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:158
msgid "Let's send messages to ROS using the `Key Publisher` an Gazebo plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:160
msgid ""
"**Note:** Make sure to have all workspaces you need (ROS, Gazebo and, "
"`ros_gz`...) sourced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:163
msgid ""
"First we will start a bridge between ROS and Gazebo specifying the topic at "
"which the `Key Publisher` plugin sends messages and also the type of the "
"messages as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:167
msgid ""
"ros2 run ros_gz_bridge parameter_bridge /keyboard/keypress@std_msgs/msg/"
"Int32@gz.msgs.Int32\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_integration.md:171
msgid ""
"We started a bridge on `/keyboard/keypress` topic with message of type "
"`Int32`. For ROS it is `std_msgs/msg/Int32` and for Gazebo it is `gz.msgs."
"Int32`"
msgstr ""

